// Title: Shell Execution via Git - Linux
// Sigma ID: 47b3bbd4-1bf7-48cc-84ab-995362aaa75a
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Li Ling, Andy Parkidomo, Robert Rakowski, Blake Hartstein (Bloomberg L.P.)
// Date: 2024-09-02 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects the use of the "git" utility to execute a shell. Such behavior may be associated with
//   privilege escalation, unauthorized command execution, or to break out from restricted
//   environments.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/git/#shell
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_git_shell_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/git" and (InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains " -p " and InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains "help") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "bash 0<&1" or ProcessCommandLine contains "dash 0<&1" or ProcessCommandLine contains "sh 0<&1")
